    595  530a							; BeatTick, first: a keytar beat clock came in
    596  530a				   BeatFollow
    597  530a					      subroutine
    598  530a							; following the keytar: the beat runs on by itself, and each of its beat
    599  530a							; clocks corrects it. k = steps of this beat already played:
    600  530a							;   0		the clock is ahead of us: this beat starts now
    601  530a							;   1 .. spb/2  we're in step: the rest of the beat counts from the clock
    602  530a							;   more	 the clock is early: skip to the next beat, starting now
    603  530a							; (After a keytar Start, step 1 waits for the first clock: beatWait.)
    604  530a		       ad 06 c6 	      lda	beatWait
    605  530d		       f0 11		      beq	.flag
